From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(fusion): the model directory now matches the layout LM
 Studio indexes

LM Studio only indexes <models-dir>/<publisher>/<repo>/file.gguf - exactly two levels.
The four Bonsai packs sat one level deep in Bonsai-2-27B/, so the app reported nothing
while the sibling SC117/, ISTA-DASLab/ and ggml-org/ folders all appeared.

lms ls went from 4 models / 28.64 GB with no Bonsai to 8 models / 57.46 GB including
ternary-bonsai-2-27b, ternary-bonsai-2-27b-derisked,
ternary-bonsai-2-27b-uncensored-heretic and bonsai-2-27b-ternary-crack.

The packs are from four different Hugging Face publishers (named in
scripts/download-bonsai.sh), so each got its own publisher/repo folder rather than a
shared one; while they briefly shared prism-ml/, lms labelled them all by that path.

start-bonsai.bat moved with the official pack and now derives its model path from
%~dp0, so the next rename cannot break it. Verified: --list sees ROCm0, --cli answers
correctly, and the resolved path is the new one.

Still open: no mmproj-*.gguf, so the vision tower is unavailable - the sibling models
both ship one.
---
 fusion/state.json | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fusion/state.json b/fusion/state.json
index 5a56ccd..585a7b0 100644
--- a/fusion/state.json
+++ b/fusion/state.json
@@ -198,7 +198,7 @@
     "gpuArchitecture": "gfx1030",
     "rocm": "7.1"
   },
-  "updatedAt": "2026-09-19T19:45:00+08:00",
+  "updatedAt": "2026-09-19T20:05:00+08:00",
   "buildRecommendation": {
     "faAllQuants": "Either. Correctness was previously thought to depend on this; it does not - both configurations now measure 6.94-7.13 across the whole K/V matrix and both pass test-backend-ops FLASH_ATTN_EXT with zero failures. ON compiles every combination (447 s full rebuild, and no silent f16 fallback for exotic pairs); OFF compiles four plus the TurboQuant instances (much shorter build). This worktree is currently left ON.",
     "hipGraphs": "GGML_HIP_GRAPHS is ON in this CMakeCache and the define is present in build.ninja (154 references), so unlike an earlier note it is NOT inert. It is also not a factor: running with GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1 reproduced the 307 failures byte-identically.",
@@ -207,9 +207,10 @@
   },
   "scope": {
     "targetModel": "Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B (PrismML ternary PQ2_0, qwen35 arch, head_dim 256)",
-    "launcher": "<MODELS>/Bonsai-2-27B/start-bonsai.bat",
+    "launcher": "<MODELS>/prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf/start-bonsai.bat",
     "kvConfig": "The launcher does not pass -ctk/-ctv, so the model runs on the default f16 KV cache.",
-    "consequence": "f16 x f16 is healthy in every configuration measured, and after the dequantize_q8_0 fix every other K/V combination is too. The one remaining unverified item is turbo KV at head_dim 128, which is outside this model's geometry (key_length 256)."
+    "consequence": "f16 x f16 is healthy in every configuration measured, and after the dequantize_q8_0 fix every other K/V combination is too. The one remaining unverified item is turbo KV at head_dim 128, which is outside this model's geometry (key_length 256).",
+    "launcherNote": "moved 2026-09-19 when the pack was put into the LM-Studio-indexable two-level layout; the launcher now derives its model path from %~dp0"
   },
   "lastValidation": {
     "date": "2026-09-19",
@@ -346,5 +347,31 @@
     "what": "port PrismML private types (PQ2_0 142 / PTQ1_0 143: block layout, CPU codec, MMQ/MMVQ/MMF kernels, dequantize, convert tables) onto the upstream b11046 base, so Bonsai also rides the newer upstream",
     "whyNotBackward": "moving b11046 back to the PrismML base (merge-base b10615-1) would drop 430 upstream commits, of which 35 touch ggml/src/ggml-cuda and 75 touch src/ - including FA correctness fixes (b74f590ea fix divergent barrier in f16 flash attention) and the BF16-acceleration fallback (ad6c66839) that gfx1030 needs. That is pure regression.",
     "cost": "a real porting job, but the same shape as the one already done twice, and the audit script now exists to prove nothing is silently dropped"
+  },
+  "modelLayout": {
+    "why": "LM Studio only indexes <models-dir>/<publisher>/<repo>/file.gguf - exactly two levels. A file one level deep is not indexed and the app reports nothing, which is why the four Bonsai packs were invisible while the sibling SC117/, ISTA-DASLab/ and ggml-org/ folders all appeared.",
+    "modelsRoot": "<MODELS>, reached two ways: the junction <STACK>/models and the symlink <HOME>/.lmstudio/models -> /f/AI/lm-models",
+    "before": "<MODELS>/Bonsai-2-27B/{4 .gguf, start-bonsai.bat}   (one level - not indexed)",
+    "after": {
+      "prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf": [
+        "Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0.gguf",
+        "start-bonsai.bat"
+      ],
+      "OS-Software/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-Uncensored-Heretic-GGUF": [
+        "Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-Uncensored-Heretic-PQ2_0.gguf"
+      ],
+      "dealignai/Bonsai-2-27B-Ternary-CRACK-GGUF": [
+        "Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0-CRACK.gguf"
+      ],
+      "Blackfrost-AI/TERNARY-BONSAI-2-27B-DERISKED-GGUF": [
+        "TERNARY-BONSAI-2-27B-DERISKED-PQ2_0.gguf"
+      ]
+    },
+    "whyFourRepos": "the four packs are from four different Hugging Face publishers, named in temp_clean_later/scripts/download-bonsai.sh. When all four were briefly placed under prism-ml/ as one repo, lms ls labelled them all by the shared publisher path; after the split each gets its own model name.",
+    "proof": "lms ls before: 4 models, 28.64 GB, no Bonsai. After: 8 models, 57.46 GB, including ternary-bonsai-2-27b, ternary-bonsai-2-27b-derisked, ternary-bonsai-2-27b-uncensored-heretic and bonsai-2-27b-ternary-crack.",
+    "launcher": "start-bonsai.bat now derives its model path from %~dp0, so a future rename of the publisher/repo folders cannot break it again.",
+    "movedWith": "temp_clean_later/scripts/restructure-bonsai-layout.py (same-volume renames only, sizes verified, idempotent)",
+    "open": "no mmproj-*.gguf is present, so the vision tower is unavailable. The upstream repo ships it; LM Studio would auto-pair an mmproj file placed in the same repo folder.",
+    "date": "2026-09-19"
   }
 }
